  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access andAwareness  Hygiene Sanitation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is planned to start from March 2024 and end by December 2026 (34 Months) and implemented in 13 communes within 08 district in two selected provinces, Battambang and Siem Reap. TS1001 will ensure the establishment and functional operation of 10 sustainable Water Kiosks (WKs) in 10 selected communes, 05 in Siem Reap in year 1 and 05 in Battambang in year 2. 08 will be funded by KOICA while the other 02 will be co-funded by the project. These WKs create local job for at least 10 WK entrepreneurs who will be ableto deliver safe drinking water to approximately 30,0000 people3, including school children. At the means time, HURREDO will ensure the promotion of sanitation in 08 target communes (05 in Siem Reap and 03 in Battambang), aiming at increasing number of villages with Open Defecation Free (ODF) and access to improved latrine through different behavior change events and capacity building. To ensure the project intervention benefiting vulnerable groups, especially women and PWD, Oxfam in Cambodia will strengthen the capacity of ST1001, HURREDO and other key stakeholders on gender equality and inclusion. Oxfam will also engage with different private sector stakeholders to engage in WASH innovation events. At the national level, Oxfam will also actively coordinate multi-stakeholders events with the government and other WASH actors in the country for information dissemination and advocacy purposes. It is anticipated that, by the end of the project, approximately 106,455 people (including 53,722female and girls) will directly benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HURREDO is a local Cambodian non-profit organization that works to alleviate poverty and helps rural communities to create a sustainable future. The organization was set up in 1999 by a group of Cambodian agriculture and rural development specialists whowere passionate about creating a brighter future for the rural communities of Cambodia. On January 19th, 2000 HURREDO was officially recognized and registered with the Ministry of Interior and since then the NGO has been working hard with the Royal Government of Cambodia and other NGOs to improve the living standards of Cambodians</narrative>
